  "claims": [
    "CertifiedComparison preserves instance families, packaged adversary/witness outputs, actual emitted programs, resource certificates, and pointwise advantage-loss functions.",
    "The existing condition-bearing directed Plan/Cell syntax has a checked computational interpretation. Atomic rules carry genuine CertifiedReductions; local higher rules must prove CertifiedComparison.",
    "Structural laws and pasting preserve computational comparison; whole-diagram condition repair reconstructs comparison in the checked updated model.",
    "A restricted PRG-encryption branch presentation supplies all local diamonds. The previous terminalCoherence generator compares every terminal plan with the direct compiler route.",
    "For any terminal proof in each PRG branch, emitted masking code and the original all-challenge stopping guarantee are preserved; time is 2*n + 10*L(n) + 9 + t(n), polynomial under the original time/width hypotheses.",
    "Combining any two terminal branch proofs with the existing triangle theorem reconstructs the encryption 2*epsilon bound and asymptotic security under the explicit original PRG resource-class assumption.",
    "A counterexample uses identical certified programs/packets and a balanced charge multiset, but two negligible-preserving loss functions compose differently. No computational HigherModel can interpret that charge-balanced rule with the exhibited base model."
  ],
