  "scope": [
    "This is a computational interpretation, not a coupling or equality theorem for real/ideal challenge distributions. Statistical state kernels are neither inferred nor discarded.",
    "Computational loss functions are checked explicitly; a commutative multiset of additive error IDs does not determine their composition.",
    "The PRG terminal graph has three vertices, exact uniform-pad rewrite, computational replacement, and a direct route built from the same certified reduction with the identity compiler node removed. This is not an independent stronger reduction or machine optimization.",
    "The named example condition is the exact uniform-pad observation equality. The actual PRG boundedness/security hypothesis remains an explicit terminal premise, not an automatically extracted changed condition.",
    "The PRG backend stores its time profile in the security object, with Unit resource payload. The halts and time_polynomial theorems expose the real budget; Unit is not reported as a numerical resource profile.",
    "Current execution transfer is for the existing masking backend. The separate complete native query/loading backend is not newly connected by this example.",
    "The loss obstruction is an intentionally loose certificate on a zero observation, with finite-prefix additive error. It disproves automatic preservation of assigned loss functions, not equality of actual success probabilities or possibility of a tighter bound.",
    "Full mixed coherence with cyclic exchanges/copy/discard, an elementary finite basis, proof-sharing cost comparison, and publication novelty remain open."
  ],
